<title>USA: Teva's Pindolo drug gets FDA approval.</title>
<headline>Teva's Pindolo drug gets FDA approval.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd said Friday it had received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) to make and market Pindolol tablets.</p>
<p>Pindolol is the generic equivalent of Sandoz AG's Visken, a drug for the treatment of hypertension, it said, adding that there were several generic versions of the product available.</p>
<p>Teva makes branded and generic pharmaceutical products.</p>
</text>
